Stopped believing `X-Forwarded-For` by default when working out a visitor's address, because a client can send that header to any site, write what it likes into the audit log, and take a fresh magic-link rate-limit bucket on every request. The address now comes from `request.getClientAddr()`, which honours Zope's `trusted-proxy` setting, unless the site names a header in the new `client_ip_headers` setting. A site behind a proxy has to do one or the other, or the audit log records the proxy's address and every visitor shares one rate-limit bucket. Upgrade step 1012 creates the setting, empty. `client_ip` moved from `pas.plugins.identity.core.services.magiclink` to `pas.plugins.identity.core.utils.clientip`. @ericof
